Temporary trace confirmed supplemental GS selection even for both shader
clip-distance draws. AMD_DEBUG=initnir,vs,gs,nongg showed the user vertex
shader has next_stage=MESA_SHADER_FRAGMENT and its CLIP_DIST0 store is marked
no_varying. The separately bound GS loads VARYING_SLOT_CLIP_DIST0. Thus the
supplemental GS cannot assume that the shader's clip distance is exported as
a varying after the program was linked without a GS. See full NIR dump.

All physical tests completed below their timeouts. Kernel journal filtered
from first point GPU test to the last combined test showed no GPU reset, ring
timeout or fault. Installed Mesa afterwards: direct rendering Yes, AMD radeonsi,
Mesa 25.2.8-0ubuntu0.24.04.4.
Private st_draw.c and libgallium were restored byte-for-byte to pre-test state.
